  = note: C99 §5.2.4.1: this implementation limits an object to PTRDIFF_MAX bytes so that pointer differences within it are representable (§6.5.6p9)

error: enumeration values have no common supported integer type: `huge`
 --> sema-int128-constraints.c:3:19
  |
3 | enum OutOfRange { huge = (__uint128_t)-1 };
  |                   ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ no supported enum type holds this value with the others
  |
  = note: C99 §6.7.2.2p4: an enumerated type is compatible with an integer type that represents every member; this implementation requires a common type of at most 64 bits

